n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(y+3z)}^{9},$ we have $a=y,$ $b=3z,$ and $n=9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(y+3z)}^{9}=(\\frac{9}{0}){y}^{9}(3z)^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){y}^{9-1}(3z)^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){y}^{9-2}(3z)^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{9}{9}){y}^{9-9}(3z)^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${y}^{6}{z}^{3}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{9}{3}){y}^{9-3}(3z)^{3}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{9}{3}){y}^{9-3}(3z)^{3} & =84{y}^{6}\\cdot {3}^{3}{z}^{3} \\\\  & =84{y}^{6}\\cdot 27{z}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\,268{y}^{6}{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${y}^{6}{z}^{3}$ is $2\\,268.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/state.json" "file_sha256" "852634ef6e7f62cba2b131730816f1a94a75970c2e3507b71abae2600247adaf"} {"question" "q-113625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cedad404b947dcd4b461bd2c511fd0b1c79556cfa346f0e8fc0f3d13aacc2120"} {"question" "q-113625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/state.json" "file_sha256" "852634ef6e7f62cba2b131730816f1a94a75970c2e3507b71abae2600247adaf"} {"question" "q-113625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13\\,608"] ["math" "2\\,268"] ["math" "504"] ["math" "756"] ["math" "84"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/state.json" "file_sha256" "852634ef6e7f62cba2b131730816f1a94a75970c2e3507b71abae2600247adaf"} {"question" "q-113625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,268"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/state.json" "file_sha256" "852634ef6e7f62cba2b131730816f1a94a75970c2e3507b71abae2600247adaf"} {"question" "q-18624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The coefficient of ${x}^{12}$ in the expansion of ${(2+x)}^{15}$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/state.json" "file_sha256" "852634ef6e7f62cba2b131730816f1a94a75970c2e3507b71abae2600247adaf"} {"question" "q-18624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(2+x)}^{15},$ we have $a=2,$ $b=x,$ and $n=15.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+x)^{15}=(\\frac{15}{0}){2}^{15}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{15}{1}){2}^{15-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{15}{2}){2}^{15-2}{x}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{15}{15}){2}^{15-15}{x}^{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{12}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{15}{12}){2}^{15-12}{x}^{12}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{15}{12}){2}^{15-12} & =455\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =455\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =3\\,640.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{12}$ is $3\\,640.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/state.json" "file_sha256" "852634ef6e7f62cba2b131730816f1a94a75970c2e3507b71abae2600247adaf"} {"question" "q-18624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13988467/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cedad404b947dcd4b461bd2c511fd0b1c79556cfa346f0e8fc0f3d13aacc2120"